From dfbf0c93e27f85e48752fcec49d94082156f7904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:40:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: eon: enable dual output read on EN25QH32

The EN25QH32 supports the 1-1-2 Dual Output Fast Read (3Bh), as its
EN25QH16 and EN25QH64 siblings already declare. Declare it here too, so
boards that wire the two data lines at a wider bus width read twice as
fast.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
index a3b57a687..8332dada9 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/eon.c
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ static const struct flash_info eon_nor_parts[] = {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x16),
 		.name = "en25qh32",
 		.size = SZ_4M,
+		.no_sfdp_flags = SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ,
 	}, {
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0x1c, 0x70, 0x17),
 		.name = "en25qh64",
-- 
2.43.0

